      "decision_index": 185,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "At 1 life facing lethal attacks from Enduring Innocence, activating Cori Mountain Monastery's expensive ability (costing 4 mana + tap) leaves only 2 untapped lands, making it impossible to cast the critical Day of Judgment ({2}{W}{W}) this turn. The opponent can simply attack for lethal next combat.",
      "action_taken": "Activated Cori Mountain Monastery's {3}{R},{T} ability to exile and potentially play the top card of library.",
      "better_line": "Cast Day of Judgment immediately to clear Enduring Innocence and survive. At 1 life, board-wiping is the only priority - a random exiled card is far less important than staying alive.",
